#!/bin/bash
# RDP Link installer: allow the host through the Application Firewall and
# install the login service for the console user. Privacy permissions still
# require the user's one-time approval (macOS rule); the Setup assistant
# guides that after launch.
set -e

APP="/Applications/RDP Link.app"
AGENT="$APP/Contents/MacOS/office-rdp"

if [ -x "$AGENT" ]; then
  /usr/libexec/ApplicationFirewall/socketfilterfw --add "$AGENT" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
  /usr/libexec/ApplicationFirewall/socketfilterfw --unblockapp "$AGENT" >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
fi

CONSOLE_USER="$(stat -f%Su /dev/console)"
if [ -n "$CONSOLE_USER" ] && [ "$CONSOLE_USER" != "root" ] && [ -x "$AGENT" ]; then
  sudo -u "$CONSOLE_USER" "$AGENT" --install-service >/dev/null 2>&1 || true
fi

exit 0
